## ⚠️ Limitations

This project uses **synthetic data** generated for educational purposes, covering roughly 90 days of transactions. `Risk_Review_Flag` is an illustrative label, not a real fraud or compliance determination, and findings here are not intended to reflect real-world banking risk patterns. The final model's precision (~26%) means most flags are false alarms — acceptable for a manual-review triage tool, not for an automated blocking decision. The model also under-performs on smaller, daytime, non-Transfer transactions. No official output from other FinTrust tracks (Data Analytics, ML Engineering, etc.) was available during this project, so no actual cross-track integration occurred — this is documented directly rather than overstated. Full detail on all assumptions and limitations is in each week's report.

